{"id": "6e6e9dc6-c5d8-45c0-88ca-b8fe2c73a887", "card": {"foregroundColor": {"blue": 1, "green": 1, "opacity": 1, "red": 1}, "image": "", "imageStyle": "textFirst", "localizedTitle": {"en": "### Windy city", "es": "### Windy City", "pt": "### Windy City"}}, "pages": [{"id": "290e5667-d330-4ad4-b516-d32102aa5c98", "blocks": [{"id": "efe5a2e1-b126-4725-82d9-2e36ccd33ef4", "backgroundTransparent": true, "localizedText": {"en": "## Windy City", "es": "## Windy City", "pt": "## Windy City"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": true}, {"id": "8cfaf30e-9197-466f-9441-030d608de1c1", "coordinateRegion": {"latitude": 41.87431178109076, "latitudinalMeters": 90978.43009227383, "longitude": -87.55623135109022, "longitudinalMeters": 182637.13705380648}, "height": "regular", "type": "map"}, {"id": "f8486422-30df-47b3-a6b0-2e232e352bd7", "backgroundTransparent": false, "localizedText": {"en": "**Friday, March 26, at 1 pm**\n\nOn this day in the Chicago (USA) area, the wind speed was 5 mph at 1 pm, then lowered to 1 mph at 3 pm before increasing again to 7.8 mph at 9 pm.", "es": "**Viernes 26 de Marzo, a las 13:00**\n\nEn este d\u00eda, en el \u00e1rea de Chicago (EE.\u00a0UU.), la velocidad del viento era de 5\u00a0mph a las 13:00, luego baj\u00f3 a 1\u00a0mph a las 15:00 para aumentar de nuevo a 7.8\u00a0mph a las 21:00", "pt": "**Sexta\u2011feira, 26 de mar\u00e7o, \u00e0s 13\u202fh**\n\nNeste dia, na regi\u00e3o de Chicago (EUA), a velocidade do vento era de 5\u202fmph \u00e0s 13\u202fh, caiu para 1\u202fmph \u00e0s 15\u202fh e depois aumentou novamente para 7,8\u202fmph \u00e0s 21\u202fh."}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false}, {"id": "2525fed7-a099-4438-8734-6d0c726caffe", "octavesHigher": 512, "type": "localWave", "volumeModifier": "fixed", "waveData": {"duration": 28800, "startDate": "2021-03-26T18:00:00Z", "station": {"group": "example", "id": "3CCF5D30-6F15-4D16-98AC-7F02934AFDDE", "latitude": 39.72, "longitude": -91.51, "name": "Illinois", "periods": [{"channel": "BHZ", "from": "2011-10-10T00:00:00Z", "location": "--", "network": "TA", "station": "L44A", "to": "2015-10-16T18:00:00Z"}, {"channel": "HHZ", "from": "2015-10-16T18:00:00Z", "location": "--", "network": "TA", "station": "L44A", "to": "2019-03-14T19:55:00Z"}, {"channel": "HHZ", "from": "2019-03-15T01:09:00Z", "location": "00", "network": "NW", "station": "L44A"}], "preferredTimeZone": {"identifier": "GMT", "style": "byGMTValue"}, "timeLatency": 24}, "timeZone": {"identifier": "America/Chicago", "style": "byName"}}}, {"id": "09bde3fe-2e6d-48ff-b484-10fae083185f", "backgroundTransparent": false, "localizedText": {"en": "**Monday, March 29, at 1 pm**\n\nThe following Monday, the wind speed was 19.7 mph at 1 pm, then increased to 28 mph at 9 pm.", "es": "**Lunes 29 de Marzo, a las 13:00**\n\nEl lunes siguiente, la velocidad del viento era de 19,7\u00a0mph a las 13:00 y aument\u00f3 a 28\u00a0mph a las 21:00", "pt": "**Segunda\u2011feira, 29 de mar\u00e7o, \u00e0s 13\u202fh**\n\nNa segunda seguinte, a velocidade do vento era de 19,7\u202fmph \u00e0s 13\u202fh e aumentou para 28\u202fmph \u00e0s 21\u202fh."}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false}, {"id": "57403514-c291-44be-a0ea-97390f001a80", "octavesHigher": 512, "type": "localWave", "volumeModifier": "fixed", "waveData": {"duration": 28800, "startDate": "2021-03-29T18:00:00Z", "station": {"group": "example", "id": "3CCF5D30-6F15-4D16-98AC-7F02934AFDDE", "latitude": 39.72, "longitude": -91.51, "name": "Illinois", "periods": [{"channel": "BHZ", "from": "2011-10-10T00:00:00Z", "location": "--", "network": "TA", "station": "L44A", "to": "2015-10-16T18:00:00Z"}, {"channel": "HHZ", "from": "2015-10-16T18:00:00Z", "location": "--", "network": "TA", "station": "L44A", "to": "2019-03-14T19:55:00Z"}, {"channel": "HHZ", "from": "2019-03-15T01:09:00Z", "location": "00", "network": "NW", "station": "L44A"}], "preferredTimeZone": {"identifier": "GMT", "style": "byGMTValue"}, "timeLatency": 24}, "timeZone": {"identifier": "America/Chicago", "style": "byName"}}}, {"id": "0e740015-cb55-4be2-b201-d4ae8c68fc4b", "backgroundTransparent": false, "localizedText": {"en": "You should hear louder seismic noise for the day with the higher wind speeds,\nbecause wind doesn\u2019t just push on us, our structures, trees, and topography\nbut also directly and indirectly on the ground. Remember that you can choose\nto adjust the volume. When you do that the volume adjusts automatically to\nassign the loudest sound to the largest wave signal.\n", "es": "Deber\u00edas escuchar un ruido s\u00edsmico m\u00e1s fuerte durante el d\u00eda con las velocidades\ndel viento m\u00e1s altas, porque el viento no solo nos empuja a nosotros, a las\nestructuras, los \u00e1rboles y la topograf\u00eda, sino tambi\u00e9n, directa e indirectamente,\nal suelo. Recuerda que puedes ajustar el volumen. Cuando lo haces, el volumen\nse ajusta autom\u00e1ticamente para asignar el sonido m\u00e1ximo a la se\u00f1al de onda\nm\u00e1s grande.\n", "pt": "Voc\u00ea deve ouvir um ru\u00eddo s\u00edsmico mais alto no dia com velocidades do vento\nmaiores, pois o vento n\u00e3o empurra apenas a n\u00f3s, nossas estruturas, \u00e1rvores\ne relevo, mas tamb\u00e9m, direta e indiretamente, o solo. Lembre\u2011se de que voc\u00ea\npode ajustar o volume. Ao fazer isso, o volume \u00e9 ajustado automaticamente\npara atribuir o som mais alto ao maior sinal de onda.\n"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false}, {"id": "bafc18c6-0a29-430f-b5e5-7c6139bab7c0", "backgroundTransparent": true, "localizedText": {"en": "## Questions", "es": "## Preguntas", "pt": "## Perguntas"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": true}, {"id": "4f9dcc96-b104-4980-bd2f-f123d540b6e2", "backgroundTransparent": false, "localizedText": {"en": "**Question 1.** Do you think the more windy day will still sound a bit\nlouder than the less windy day?\n", "es": "**Pregunta 1.** \u00bfCrees que el d\u00eda con m\u00e1s viento sonar\u00e1 un poco m\u00e1s fuerte que el d\u00eda con\nmenos viento?\n", "pt": "**Pergunta 1.** Voc\u00ea acha que o dia com mais vento ainda soar\u00e1 um pouco mais alto do que o\ndia menos com menos vento?\n"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false}, {"id": "e33ec1c4-3637-470d-ad5c-56c06ee17a90", "backgroundTransparent": true, "localizedText": {"en": "No, the loudness is auto-adjusted and no longer reflects the intensity of the signal.\n", "es": "No, el volumen se ajusta autom\u00e1ticamente y ya no refleja la intensidad de la se\u00f1al.\n", "pt": "N\u00e3o, o volume \u00e9 ajustado automaticamente e n\u00e3o reflete mais a intensidade do sinal.\n"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false, "unveil": {"unveilText": {"en": "Unveil answer", "es": "Desvelar respuesta", "pt": "Revelar resposta"}, "waitingTime": 5}}, {"id": "de06c564-fbc2-425e-be51-202dcd8eb1ca", "backgroundTransparent": false, "localizedText": {"en": "**Question 2.** Try it out by touching the circular button to the bottom left of the signal. \nCan you explain the difference in loudness?\n", "es": "**Pregunta 2.** Pru\u00e9balo tocando el bot\u00f3n circular en la parte inferior izquierda de la\nse\u00f1al. \u00bfPuedes explicar la diferencia de volumen?\n", "pt": "**Pergunta 2.** Experimente tocar o bot\u00e3o circular no canto inferior esquerdo do sinal. \nVoc\u00ea consegue explicar a diferen\u00e7a de volume?\n"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false}, {"id": "4caffbb7-190f-45e9-9aee-c56760abe79b", "backgroundTransparent": true, "localizedText": {"en": "With the fixed volume settings, we can hear louder seismic noise on the windier day \nthan on the less windy day. With auto-adjusted volume that difference is removed, \nbut it allows us to hear different characteristics of the noise.\n", "es": "Con los ajustes de volumen fijo, podemos escuchar m\u00e1s ruido s\u00edsmico en el d\u00eda m\u00e1s \nventoso que en el d\u00eda menos ventoso. Con el volumen autoajustado, esa diferencia se \nelimina, pero nos permite escuchar diferentes caracter\u00edsticas del ruido.\n", "pt": "Com as configura\u00e7\u00f5es de volume fixo, conseguimos ouvir mais ru\u00eddo s\u00edsmico no dia\ncom mais vento do que no dia com menos vento. Com o volume autoajustado essa diferen\u00e7a\ndesaparece, mas permite que ou\u00e7amos diferentes caracter\u00edsticas do ru\u00eddo.\n"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false, "unveil": {"unveilText": {"en": "Unveil answer", "es": "Desvelar respuesta", "pt": "Revelar resposta"}, "waitingTime": 5}}, {"id": "164eb891-900a-4565-8cdf-1310fc7d41a5", "action": "next", "localizedText": {"en": "Next", "es": "Siguiente", "pt": "Pr\u00f3ximo"}, "paramValue": "", "type": "button"}], "title": "Windy city"}, {"id": "66d3f308-f023-4395-99d9-3584890c511b", "blocks": [{"id": "1dfa1358-5395-4723-b472-66416f4c4a0b", "backgroundTransparent": true, "localizedText": {"en": "## Windy City (II)", "es": "## Windy City (II)", "pt": "## Windy City (II)"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": true}, {"id": "0bf08b84-a375-4e47-bb10-d0b15ff8d823", "height": "regular", "image": "", "type": "image"}, {"id": "748ba012-0c4b-4649-ab53-b8dd38389ff7", "backgroundTransparent": false, "localizedText": {"en": "Not all of the noise you hear is related to wind. Some of it is steady\nbackground noise generated by the oceans.\n\n> Yes, even in Illinois we can hear it because seismic waves propagate \n  very efficiently -and fast!- through the solid Earth.\n\nThere are also signals buried in the noise that are from distant earthquakes \nthat are so weak you cannot hear them. But, if you speed the sound up more, \nusing octaves higher to 14, you can hear their unique low frequency waves as \n\u201cpings\u201d.\n", "es": "No todo el ruido que escuchas est\u00e1 relacionado con el viento. Parte del\nruido constante de fondo es generado por los oc\u00e9anos.\n\n> S\u00ed, incluso en Illinois podemos escucharlo porque las ondas s\u00edsmicas se\n  propagan de manera muy eficiente -\u00a1y r\u00e1pida!- a trav\u00e9s de la Tierra s\u00f3lida.\n\nTambi\u00e9n hay se\u00f1ales escondidas en el ruido que provienen de terremotos lejanos\nque son tan d\u00e9biles que no se pueden o\u00edr. Pero, si aceleras m\u00e1s el sonido,\nusando un incremento de octavas de 14, puedes escuchar sus ondas de baja frecuencia\n\u00fanicas como *pings*.\n", "pt": "Nem todo o ru\u00eddo que voc\u00ea ouve est\u00e1 relacionado ao vento. Parte dele \u00e9 um\nru\u00eddo de fundo constante gerado pelos oceanos.\n\n> Sim, mesmo em Illinois conseguimos ouvir isso porque as ondas s\u00edsmicas\n  se propagam de forma muito eficiente \u2013 e r\u00e1pida! \u2013 atrav\u00e9s da Terra s\u00f3lida.\n\nH\u00e1 tamb\u00e9m sinais escondidos no ru\u00eddo provenientes de terremotos distantes\nt\u00e3o fracos que voc\u00ea n\u00e3o consegue ouvi\u2011los. Mas, se voc\u00ea acelerar ainda mais\no som, usando o ajuste de 14 oitavas acima, poder\u00e1 ouvir suas ondas \u00fanicas\nde baixa frequ\u00eancia como \u201cpings\u201d.\n"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false}, {"id": "1eb52918-3ab0-4630-aad3-1d6baf1c04cc", "backgroundTransparent": true, "localizedText": {"en": "> **Note:** Swipe right to go back to the previous page.\n", "es": "> **Nota:** Desliza el dedo hacia la derecha para volver a la p\u00e1gina anterior.\n", "pt": "> **Observa\u00e7\u00e3o:** Deslize para a direita para voltar \u00e0 p\u00e1gina anterior.\n"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false}, {"id": "656e413c-8c46-4587-a144-d065641a0f87", "backgroundTransparent": false, "localizedText": {"en": "For the less windy day, you can hear a clear quake signal (when octaves\nhigher by 14) in the middle of the record, which is from a M5.9 quake near\nHirara, Japan.\n\nAn hour earlier there is a much fainter signal from a M5.8 quake on the \nPacific-Antarctic Ridge in the South Pacific Ocean.\n", "es": "En el d\u00eda menos ventoso, puedes escuchar una clara se\u00f1al de terremoto (cuando\nel incremento de octavas es 14) en el medio de la onda. Es de un terremoto\nM5.9 ocurrido cerca de Hirara, Jap\u00f3n.\n\nUna hora antes, hab\u00eda una se\u00f1al mucho m\u00e1s d\u00e9bil de un terremoto M5.8 en la\nCordillera Pac\u00edfico-Ant\u00e1rtica, en el Oc\u00e9ano Pac\u00edfico Sur.\n", "pt": "No dia com menos vento, voc\u00ea pode ouvir um sinal de terremoto claro (com\n14 oitavas acima) no meio do registro, proveniente de um terremoto M5.9\npr\u00f3ximo a Hirara, no Jap\u00e3o.\n\nUma hora antes h\u00e1 um sinal bem mais fraco de um terremoto M5.8 na Dorsal\nPac\u00edfico\u2011Ant\u00e1rtica, no Oceano Pac\u00edfico Sul.\n"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false}, {"id": "87323282-7a92-4aa6-9f6d-b61370c9c0cb", "backgroundTransparent": true, "localizedText": {"en": "## Question", "es": "## Pregunta", "pt": "## Pergunta"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": true}, {"id": "b9d83e8d-85d4-4dee-916e-14be5458d001", "backgroundTransparent": false, "localizedText": {"en": "**Question 1.** Given that the magnitudes differ by only 0.1 (40% in energy or 12% in slip\nand fault length and width), **why do you think the signal sounds so much\nmore faint?**\n", "es": "**Pregunta 1.** Dado que las magnitudes difieren solo en 0,1 (40\u00a0% en energ\u00eda o 12\u00a0% en\ndeslizamiento y en el largo y ancho de la falla), **\u00bfpor qu\u00e9 crees que la\nse\u00f1al suena mucho m\u00e1s d\u00e9bil?**\n", "pt": "**Pergunta 1.** Considerando que as magnitudes diferem apenas em 0,1 (40\u202f% em energia ou\n12\u202f% em deslocamento e no comprimento e largura da falha), **por que voc\u00ea\nacha que o sinal soa t\u00e3o mais fraco?**\n"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false}, {"id": "4c9323b4-ddea-4f77-9d62-d338a59a727d", "backgroundTransparent": true, "localizedText": {"en": "Because the South Pacific Ocean is much farther from Chicago than Japan. Just like \nlight from the sun, seismic waves lose intensity as they spread out through the Earth.\n", "es": "Porque el Oc\u00e9ano Pac\u00edfico Sur est\u00e1 mucho m\u00e1s lejos de Chicago que de Jap\u00f3n. Al igual \nque la luz del sol, las ondas s\u00edsmicas pierden intensidad a medida que se dispersan a \ntrav\u00e9s de la Tierra.\n", "pt": "Porque o Oceano Pac\u00edfico Sul est\u00e1 muito mais longe de Chicago do que o Jap\u00e3o. Assim como\na luz do sol, as ondas s\u00edsmicas perdem intensidade \u00e0 medida que se espalham pela Terra.\n"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false, "unveil": {"unveilText": {"en": "Unveil answer", "es": "Desvelar respuesta", "pt": "Revelar resposta"}, "waitingTime": 5}}, {"id": "3e158b19-894f-4c5a-918b-a0461992770f", "action": "next", "localizedText": {"en": "Next", "es": "Siguiente", "pt": "Pr\u00f3ximo"}, "paramValue": "", "type": "button"}], "title": "Page 2. Info"}, {"id": "0167de40-6c13-4310-8ca1-919b90c45605", "blocks": [{"id": "b65b8dbb-ef45-4af1-8064-3461152e866f", "backgroundTransparent": true, "localizedText": {"en": "## Windy City (III)", "es": "## Windy City (III)", "pt": "## Windy City (III)"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": true}, {"id": "3c6c7077-39fe-40b2-bba4-83f7cf4e4cbc", "backgroundTransparent": false, "localizedText": {"en": "For the more windy day, the record contains three clear quake signals.\nThe first is near the beginning of the record and is from a M5.5 quake in\nwestern Xizang, Tibet. The second is still in the first half of the record\nand is from a pair of M5.1 and M5.2 quakes that occurred 2.5 minutes apart\nin the Mariana Islands region. The last one is from a M5.2 quake in the Beaufort\nSea, north of Canada.\n", "es": "Para el d\u00eda m\u00e1s ventoso, el registro contiene tres se\u00f1ales claras de terremoto.\nEl primero est\u00e1 cerca del comienzo del registro y es de un terremoto de M5.5\nen el oeste de Xizang, T\u00edbet. El segundo se encuentra en la primera mitad\ndel registro y es de un par de terremotos, M5.1 y M5.2, que ocurrieron con\n2.5 minutos de diferencia en la regi\u00f3n de las Islas Marianas. El \u00faltimo es\nde un terremoto M5.2 en el mar de Beaufort, al norte de Canad\u00e1.\n", "pt": "Para o dia com mais vento, o registro cont\u00e9m tr\u00eas sinais claros de terremoto.\nO primeiro est\u00e1 perto do in\u00edcio do registro e \u00e9 de um terremoto M5.5 no\noeste de Xizang, Tibete. O segundo ainda est\u00e1 na primeira metade do registro\ne \u00e9 de um par de terremotos M5.1 e M5.2 que ocorreram com 2,5 minutos de\ndiferen\u00e7a na regi\u00e3o das Ilhas Marianas. O \u00faltimo \u00e9 de um terremoto M5.2\nno mar de Beaufort, ao norte do Canad\u00e1.\n"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false}, {"id": "c368b5be-5de5-4aab-8083-af50f5e06b2e", "backgroundTransparent": false, "localizedText": {"en": "These quake signals are ten times less loud than the recorded Earth noise\nand thus are very hard to spot by eye. Luckily, our ears - and sophisticated\ndata analysis methods in a seismologists's toolbox - can detect these signals\ndue to the unique low frequency signals generated by these quakes.\n", "es": "Estas se\u00f1ales s\u00edsmicas son diez veces menos fuertes que el ruido de la Tierra\nregistrado y, por lo tanto, son muy dif\u00edciles de detectar a simple vista.\nAfortunadamente, nuestros o\u00eddos, y los m\u00e9todos sofisticados de an\u00e1lisis de\ndatos de los que dispone un sism\u00f3logo, pueden detectar estas se\u00f1ales gracias\na las se\u00f1ales \u00fanicas de baja frecuencia generadas por estos terremotos.\n", "pt": "Esses sinais s\u00edsmicos s\u00e3o dez vezes menos altos do que o ru\u00eddo terrestre\nregistrado e, portanto, s\u00e3o dif\u00edceis de identificar a olho nu. Felizmente,\nnossos ouvidos \u2013 e m\u00e9todos sofisticados de an\u00e1lise de dados do arsenal de\num sism\u00f3logo \u2013 podem detectar esses sinais gra\u00e7as \u00e0s suas ondas exclusivas\nde baixa frequ\u00eancia.\n"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false}, {"id": "56d17ad8-1177-4985-8088-5fa84025dbf1", "backgroundTransparent": false, "localizedText": {"en": "Earth noise never stops and creates a palette of unique sounds, ranging\nfrom eerie to annoying to fascinating. If you want to maximize the number\nof different types of sound you hear and if you have enough patience, listen\nto the records at octaves higher set to 8.\n", "es": "El ruido de la tierra nunca se detiene y crea una paleta de sonidos \u00fanicos,\nque son desde inquietantes, a molestos y a fascinantes. Si quieres maximizar\nla cantidad de diferentes tipos de sonido que se pueden escuchar y si tienes\nsuficiente paciencia, escucha los registros con el incremento de octavas a\n8.\n", "pt": "O ru\u00eddo da Terra nunca para e cria uma paleta de sons \u00fanicos, que variam desde\nassustadores at\u00e9 irritantes e fascinantes. Se voc\u00ea quiser maximizar a variedade\nde sons que ouve e tiver paci\u00eancia, escute os registros com o ajuste de 8\noitavas acima.\n"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false}, {"id": "1cc343c1-d990-4a8d-8c44-a3bac3137e88", "backgroundTransparent": false, "localizedText": {"en": "Researchers use lots of seismic signals from both earthquakes and noise\nto make three-dimensional images of the interior of the Earth. Such images\nreveal clues about the processes and forces that drive plate tectonics and\nnatural hazards, and reveal Earth's evolution over geological time. Understanding\nEarth physics and Earth's past and present helps us glimpse into the future.\n", "es": "Los investigadores utilizan muchas se\u00f1ales s\u00edsmicas tanto de terremotos\ncomo de ruido para crear im\u00e1genes tridimensionales del interior de la Tierra.\nEstas im\u00e1genes revelan pistas sobre los procesos y fuerzas que impulsan la\ntect\u00f3nica de placas y los peligros naturales y revelan la evoluci\u00f3n de la\nTierra a lo largo del tiempo geol\u00f3gico. Comprender la f\u00edsica de la Tierra,\nsu pasado y su presente nos ayuda a vislumbrar el futuro.\n", "pt": "Pesquisadores usam muitos sinais s\u00edsmicos, tanto de terremotos quanto de\nru\u00eddo, para criar imagens tridimensionais do interior da Terra. Essas\nimagens revelam pistas sobre os processos e for\u00e7as que impulsionam a\ntect\u00f4nica de placas e os perigos naturais, al\u00e9m de revelar a evolu\u00e7\u00e3o da\nTerra ao longo do tempo geol\u00f3gico. Compreender a f\u00edsica da Terra, seu passado\ne seu presente nos ajuda a vislumbrar o futuro.\n"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false}, {"id": "91f1f5a4-1bd7-40f8-985f-53db34cb2b54", "action": "close", "localizedText": {"en": "Close", "es": "Cerrar", "pt": "Fechar"}, "paramValue": "", "type": "button"}], "title": "Page 3. More questions"}], "title": {"en": "Windy city", "es": "Windy City", "pt": "Windy City"}}